[0.001, "o", "──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\r\u001b[1B← \u001b[48;2;177;185;249m\u001b[38;2;0;0;0m ☐ Rounding \u001b[39m\u001b[49m ☐ Request shape  ✔ Submit  →\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[2m│\u001b[22m \u001b[38;2;255;255;255m\u001b[1mPercentage splits often don't land on whole cents (e.g. 33.33% of 10.00). How should the leftover cents be allocated?\r\u001b[1B\u001b[22m\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;177;185;249m❯\u001b[3G\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m1.\u001b[6G\u001b[38;2;177;185;249mLargest remainder (Recommended)\r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m \u001b[3G   \u001b[38;2;153;153;153mFloor each share, then give leftover cents one each to the participants with the largest fractional remainders; ties broken by group member order. Fairest; \r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m     \u001b[38;2;153;153;153miden\u001b[11Gical to today'\u001b[26G rul\u001b[31G when pe\u001b[40Gce\u001b[43Gtages are\u001b[53Gequal.\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m2.\u001b[6G\u001b[39mMember order\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153mFloor each s"]
[0.001, "o", "hare, then give leftover cents one each to participants in group member order — exactly mirrors the existing equal-split remainder rule, but can \r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m \u001b[3G   \u001b[38;2;153;153;153mfavor early members\u001b[26Gregard\u001b[33Ge\u001b[35Gs\u001b[37Gof how\u001b[44Gclose\u001b[50Gthey were.\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m3. Type something.\r\u001b[1B──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m  4.\u001b[6GChat\u001b[11Gabout\u001b[17Gthis\r\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153mEnter to select ·\u001b[19GTab/Arrow keys to navigate\u001b[46G· Esc to cancel\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[40;1H\u001b[30;1H\u001b[?2026l"]
